169
00:18:50,378 --> 00:18:54,048
It has ever so many verses , much more than ' The Wreck of the Hesperus ' .

170
00:18:54,215 --> 00:18:55,257
Would that do ?

171
00:18:55,425 --> 00:18:57,093
What is the name of this poem ?

172
00:18:57,260 --> 00:18:59,178
' An Ode to St Valentine ' .

173
00:18:59,346 --> 00:19:01,931
I 'm not acquainted with it . Where did you find it ?

174
00:19:02,098 --> 00:19:04,809
I didn 't find it . I wrote it .

175
00:19:04,976 --> 00:19:06,477
You wrote it ?

176
00:19:08,605 --> 00:19:11,232
" Love abounds , love surrounds ... "

177
00:19:11,399 --> 00:19:15,899
Oh , no thank you , Sara . Strange as it may seem , I still prefer Mrs Heymans .

178
00:19:16,321 --> 00:19:19,949
Give me your book and proceed to recite to me as far as you have gone .

179
00:19:21,117 --> 00:19:23,077
Your book , please , Sara .

180
00:19:25,163 --> 00:19:26,289
Thank you .

181
00:19:27,540 --> 00:19:28,749
Go on .

182
00:19:29,751 --> 00:19:31,335
I can 't .

183
00:19:32,837 --> 00:19:34,421
Not one line ?

184
00:19:37,008 --> 00:19:38,884
I shall leave you now , Sara .

185
00:19:39,052 --> 00:19:43,552
I expect you to be word perfect when I send Miss Lumley in in half an hour .

186
00:19:43,807 --> 00:19:46,476
Otherwise , I 'm afraid I shall have to send you to bed

187
00:19:46,643 --> 00:19:50,313
instead of letting you stay up until the others return from the picnic .

188
00:20:03,535 --> 00:20:07,872
( WHISPERS ) Bertie ! Bertie !

189
00:20:08,957 --> 00:20:10,917
Jesus , where are you ?

190
00:20:13,461 --> 00:20:15,671
Oh , Miranda !

191
00:20:16,756 --> 00:20:18,549
( INSECTS CHIRPING )

192
00:20:24,264 --> 00:20:26,057
I like this one .

193
00:20:27,434 --> 00:20:29,936
" Shall I compare thee to a summer 's day ?

194
00:20:31,479 --> 00:20:35,979
" Thou art more lovely and more temperate .

195
00:20:36,401 --> 00:20:40,488
" Rough winds do shake the darling buds of May ,

196
00:20:40,655 --> 00:20:43,574
" And summer 's lease hath all too short a date ... "

197
00:20:43,742 --> 00:20:45,452
( CONTINUES READING SONNET )

198
00:20:45,618 --> 00:20:49,330
( MAM 'SELLE RECITING IN FRENCH )

199
00:20:49,497 --> 00:20:51,123
MR HUSSEY : That 's funny !

200
00:20:52,876 --> 00:20:55,461
Blowed if me watch hasn 't stopped .

201
00:20:57,839 --> 00:21:00,174
Dead on 12.00 .

202
00:21:04,053 --> 00:21:06,180
That 's real funny .

203
00:21:06,347 --> 00:21:07,848
( FINISHES RECITING )

204
00:21:08,016 --> 00:21:09,517
C 'est très jolie , n 'est-ce pas " ?

205
00:21:11,478 --> 00:21:15,190
You wouldn 't have the time , I suppose , miss ?

206
00:21:19,027 --> 00:21:22,739
Ah , Miranda , your pretty little diamond watch .

207
00:21:22,906 --> 00:21:24,908
Don 't wear it any more .

208
00:21:25,074 --> 00:21:27,201
Can 't stand the ticking above my heart .

209
00:21:27,368 --> 00:21:28,702
Ah !

210
00:21:29,704 --> 00:21:31,831
If it were mine ...

211
00:21:31,998 --> 00:21:36,210
I 'd wear it always , even in the bath .

212
00:21:36,377 --> 00:21:38,921
Would you , Mr Hussey ?

213
00:21:43,426 --> 00:21:46,720
Stopped at twelve .

214
00:21:46,888 --> 00:21:49,473
Never stopped before .

215
00:21:49,641 --> 00:21:51,267
Must be something magnetic .

216
00:21:51,434 --> 00:21:54,270
Well after two , I 'd say .

217
00:21:54,437 --> 00:21:56,480
We 'd better be careful .

218
00:21:56,648 --> 00:22:00,652
I promised Mrs Appleyard I 'd have you lot back at the college by eight .

219
00:22:02,195 --> 00:22:04,447
IRMA : You know what , Mam 'selle ?

220
00:22:04,614 --> 00:22:07,617
- I 'd like to go to Paris , with you . - No , no , no .

221
00:22:12,622 --> 00:22:15,666
Except for those people down there ...

222
00:22:15,834 --> 00:22:19,254
we might be the only living creatures in the whole world .

223
00:22:21,005 --> 00:22:23,048
( ETHEREAL PANPIPE MUSIC )

224
00:22:35,186 --> 00:22:37,897
- Excuse me , Mam 'selle . - Yes , Marion ?

225
00:22:38,064 --> 00:22:41,484
I should like to make a few measurements at the base of the rock if we have time .

226
00:22:41,651 --> 00:22:43,235
With Miranda and Irma .

227
00:22:46,197 --> 00:22:48,991
IRMA : Oh , please , Mam 'selle .

228
00:22:49,158 --> 00:22:51,118
We 'll be back long before tea .

229
00:22:53,705 --> 00:22:55,665
Et bien . Allez !

230
00:22:57,792 --> 00:22:59,502
May I come too , please ?

231
00:22:59,669 --> 00:23:01,921
MARION : So long as you don 't complain .

232
00:23:02,088 --> 00:23:03,714
I won 't . I promise .

233
00:23:03,882 --> 00:23:06,217
And don 't worry about us , Mam 'selle .

234
00:23:06,384 --> 00:23:08,719
We shall only be gone a little while .

235
00:23:10,722 --> 00:23:13,349
( MUSIC CONTINUES )

236
00:23:25,904 --> 00:23:27,030
Ah !

237
00:23:30,325 --> 00:23:32,118
Now I know .

238
00:23:33,328 --> 00:23:34,912
What do you know ?

239
00:23:37,123 --> 00:23:41,623
I know that Miranda is a Botticelli angel .

240
00:23:57,185 --> 00:23:58,811
( GIRLS LAUGHING )

241
00:24:06,444 --> 00:24:08,195
EDITH : Wait !

242
00:24:15,995 --> 00:24:17,663
I 'd better take a flying leap .

243
00:24:19,248 --> 00:24:21,667
- MIRANDA : Can you manage it , Edith ? - I don 't know .

244
00:24:25,046 --> 00:24:27,298
I don 't want to get my feet wet .

245
00:24:27,465 --> 00:24:28,716
( MUSIC FADES )

246
00:24:33,513 --> 00:24:35,181
Oh !

247
00:24:35,348 --> 00:24:36,682
( HE WHISTLES )

248
00:24:42,021 --> 00:24:44,648
Thought the little fat one was gonna take a bath .

249
00:24:48,569 --> 00:24:50,445
Some of them are real lookers .

250
00:24:52,031 --> 00:24:55,034
Have a look at the shape of the dark one with the curls .

251
00:24:56,035 --> 00:24:57,995
Built like an hourglass .

252
00:25:00,915 --> 00:25:03,834
And ' ave a go at the last one ! The blonde !

253
00:25:04,836 --> 00:25:07,380
Oh , she 'd have a decent pair a " legs .

254
00:25:08,923 --> 00:25:11,091
All the way up to her bum .

255
00:25:11,259 --> 00:25:14,178
I 'd rather you didn 't say crude things like that , Albert .

256
00:25:15,304 --> 00:25:19,099
I say the crude things . You just think ' em .

257
00:25:19,267 --> 00:25:20,685
EDITH : Miranda !

258
00:25:21,728 --> 00:25:23,062
Take my word for it .

259
00:25:23,229 --> 00:25:25,898
The Sheilas are all alike when it comes to fellas .

